@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-4 words; spec section 10): M18 Shutdowns (24w). The training is meeting
// train.m18.calder at the Deck 6 port junction (j); the planning screen is a new Works app tab ("Shutdowns"). Said by
// nobody unless noted; the crew's words are content/banks/m18.lines, Brennan's own in brennan.lines. Labels are short
// (buttons and headings on a phone). {where}: the branch's name from SHUT_BRANCHES ("the galley circuit"; the checker's fixed token list has no {branch}); {time}: an
// hour like 14:00; {name}: a person; {text}: the rooms it feeds, joined ("the gym and the laundry"); {n}: a count.

== works.mech.m18
- Shutdowns
== works.ask.m18
- Shutdowns | Planning one, properly. We book a real one for tomorrow together. The Deck 6 port junction, {time}, {place}.
== next.m18
- Shutdowns comes next: planning a real one with the Chief, on Deck 6.
== next.wait.m18
- Shutdowns: meet the Chief at the Deck 6 port junction.
== m18.ptr
- Shutdowns with Calder, {time}
== m18.notice
- Shutdowns with the Chief at {time}: the Deck 6 port junction. Go at quarter to.

// ---- the planning screen (the Works app's Shutdowns tab) ----
== sd.tab
- Shutdowns
== sd.none
- No jobs need a shutdown. When one does, it shows here.
== sd.head
- Jobs that need the power off
== sd.job
- {machine}: needs the power off
== sd.feeds
- Feeds
== sd.feeds.rooms
- {where}: {text}
== sd.when
- Tomorrow at
== sd.prev
- Earlier
== sd.next
- Later
== sd.who
- Who'd notice
== sd.who.none
- Nobody's in those rooms then. A quiet hour.
== sd.who.n
- {n} people in those rooms then
== sd.meal
- Mealtime: the galley needs power
== sd.class
- A class is on in one of these rooms
== sd.trad
- A ship tradition is on then
== sd.warn
- Warn
== sd.warned
- Warned
== sd.keep
- Keeps power
== sd.keep.none
- Nothing kept on
== sd.book
- Book for tomorrow
== sd.cancel
- Cancel booking
// the confirmation when you book, and when you cancel
== sd.booked
- Booked: {where}, tomorrow at {time}. It's settled at 22:00 tonight.
== sd.cancelled
- Booking cancelled. Nobody's day changes.
== sd.booked.row
- Booked: tomorrow {time}
// booking an hour that's marked (a meal, a class, a tradition): the warning on the screen
== sd.busyhour
- People will feel this one. Book it anyway?
== sd.yes
- Book it anyway
== sd.no
- Pick another hour
// a job that needs a shutdown, tapped before it's booked (the ring and the toast)
== sd.needbook
- This needs the power off. Book a shutdown first: Works app, Shutdowns.

// ---- warnings ----
// the notice on a warned person's device ({name}: you; {time}; {where})
== sd.warn.notice
- {name}: power off tomorrow, {time}, {where}. About an hour.
// the toast when you warn someone from the screen
== sd.warn.sent
- {name} is warned.
// the talk option on Brennan (and the other people who'd want telling in person)
== sd.warn.ask
- About tomorrow's shutdown

// ---- the day's Mail and the day itself ----
// 22:00 the evening before: the booking is settled (Mail, Calder; "Subject | body")
== mail.sd.settled
- Tomorrow's shutdown | Settled. {where}, {time}. The crew's day is planned round it now. Be at the junction at quarter to.
// the notice 30 minutes before, the ring at the junction, the arrow's label
== sd.notice
- Your shutdown at {time}: the junction on Deck {deck}. Go now.
== sd.ptr
- Your shutdown, {time}: switch it off
== sd.ptr.back
- Your shutdown: bring it back
// done; missed
== sd.done
- Power back on. {where} is running again.
== sd.missed
- You missed your hour. The booking's gone; the crew moved their day for nothing.
== mail.sd.missed
- Your shutdown | The hour came and went. People had moved their day for it. Book it again, and be there. I'd rather hear why from you.
// the Training tab
== m18.trained
- Shutdowns: you can book them now. Works app, Shutdowns tab.
